From: Alexandre Ferrieux <alexandre.ferrieux@orange.com>
Subject: ASoC: qcom: q6routing: map S32_LE to 24-bit for ADSP

Add S32_LE to the format switch in routing_hw_params so the routing
layer tells the ADSP to use 24-bit processing when userspace selects
S32_LE. Complements the q6asm-dai S32_LE support.

Based on postmarketOS pmaports MR !7700 for Fairphone 5 speaker support.
Co-developed-by: Bhushan Shah <bshah@kde.org>
Co-developed-by: Luca Weiss <luca.weiss@fairphone.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c	2026-03-26 19:34:37
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6routing.c	2026-03-26 19:34:57
@@ -1083,6 +1083,7 @@
 			session->bits_per_sample = 16;
 		break;
 	case SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S24_LE:
+	case SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE:
 			session->bits_per_sample = 24;
 		break;
 	default:
